"coverage":"Main Schemes 1-4 and SI preparation section pp5-25, including malic-acid-derived building blocks, recovered diastereomer inversion, acetal characterization branches and both C11 epimer routes. Nonisolated activated esters, tosylates and unprotected propargylic mixtures remain explicit operation stages unless a separately drawn numbered species is available. New benzylidene acetal configurations in control products 9a/9b remain unassigned pending independent drawing review.",
"confirmed_facts":["Triplinone F is assigned C11 R by comparison with the synthesized C11 epimer (main p3); natural-product 13C shifts were reconstructed from HSQC and recalibrated (SI p4).","SI provides the reduction/acetonide/oxidation route omitted from the main three-step arrows.","SI 6a/6b isolated yields are 40.2% and 25.8%, not 66% for each compound.","SI 7a/7b are crude products; 8a and 8b have two-step yields 94% and 88%. Main Scheme 1 separately lists rounded individual yields.","Source wavy bonds at C11 in 4, 10 and 11 are not completed to a single configuration. Ketone 12 removes this uncertainty before asymmetric reduction."],
"open_questions":["New benzylidene acetal stereocenters in characterization controls 9a/9b require an independent chair-drawing check.","The general S-series malic-acid procedure is named, but isolated yields are explicitly exemplified only for the R-series; no mirrored yield is invented."],
